1
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:03,100
"Kiss Or Kill"

2
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,000
(Episode 9)

3
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:13,519
He's not like us.

4
00:01:16,719 --> 00:01:18,200
He won't stick around.

5
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,000
Relax.

6
00:01:32,159 --> 00:01:33,718
We're not going to kill him anytime soon.

7
00:01:33,719 --> 00:01:35,439
Maybe one day when you think of it,

8
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:37,518
you can use him for a little fun.

9
00:01:37,519 --> 00:01:38,519
Whatever.

10
00:01:38,719 --> 00:01:40,055
I got bored of him a long time ago.

11
00:01:40,079 --> 00:01:42,480
I thought having him in our hands

12
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,200
was the only way to make
sure you were on my side.

13
00:01:46,159 --> 00:01:47,279
How could he possibly

14
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,839
compare to the bond between us?

15
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:49,840
Besides,

16
00:01:50,359 --> 00:01:51,920
we have mutual interests now.

17
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:57,879
I've been waiting for this day.

18
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,479
So all this time,

19
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,760
this is what you've been busy with.

20
00:02:23,599 --> 00:02:24,800
You already know,

21
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
so why ask?

22
00:02:26,159 --> 00:02:27,400
I could have helped you too.

23
00:02:28,159 --> 00:02:29,240
Why did you go to him?

24
00:02:32,199 --> 00:02:33,560
He's more useful than you.

25
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:37,639
He might help you kill Lin Cang today,

26
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:40,400
but tomorrow he'll put a knife
to your throat.

27
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,199
That's a problem for tomorrow.

28
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:46,560
Lin Yan,

29
00:02:47,039 --> 00:02:48,759
you keep saying you want revenge,

30
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:50,880
and that you'll never become him.

31
00:02:51,039 --> 00:02:52,079
But everything you're doing now,

32
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,359
isn't it exactly what he taught you?

33
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:54,479
That batch of samples,

34
00:02:54,858 --> 00:02:57,580
you tampered with it to make the
Black Moon Syndicate suspicious,

35
00:02:57,639 --> 00:02:59,240
so you could force Lin Cang to step down

36
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:01,159
and take his place legitimately.

37
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:02,560
Am I right?

38
00:03:04,439 --> 00:03:05,319
So what if you are?

39
00:03:05,319 --> 00:03:08,639
You promised me that
you wouldn't become him.

40
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,199
I am indeed different from him.

41
00:03:12,039 --> 00:03:13,479
That's why I'm going to replace him.

42
00:03:13,719 --> 00:03:16,496
You're ruthless now. What's the
difference between you and him?

43
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:18,295
Raising another batch
of killers to work for you?

44
00:03:18,319 --> 00:03:20,216
What age are you going
to start picking them from?

45
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,240
Seven?

46
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,239
Is that too old?

47
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:24,120
If he can do it,

48
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,120
why can't I?

49
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,479
That's how I was raised.

50
00:03:29,879 --> 00:03:31,079
I didn't have a choice before,

51
00:03:31,439 --> 00:03:33,759
but now I do.

52
00:03:33,879 --> 00:03:35,520
You could try to let it go

53
00:03:36,439 --> 00:03:37,679
and live a clean life.

54
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:38,680
I don't care about that.

55
00:03:40,159 --> 00:03:41,759
I want to take back what belongs to me.

56
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:53,280
I know

57
00:03:54,039 --> 00:03:55,319
you approached me from the start

58
00:03:56,919 --> 00:03:58,360
just to get something out of me.

59
00:04:01,759 --> 00:04:04,039
But I actually kind of liked you,

60
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:08,719
so it doesn't matter.

61
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:14,039
But now,

62
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,600
you're in my way,

63
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:20,199
and I can't just let that slide.

64
00:04:22,920 --> 00:04:24,319
Or you can choose to help me,

65
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:25,560
work with me.

66
00:04:26,319 --> 00:04:27,680
We can do this together.

67
00:04:29,279 --> 00:04:30,279
So,

68
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,519
you've been lying to me this whole time.

69
00:04:35,199 --> 00:04:36,600
I'm helping you.

70
00:04:38,639 --> 00:04:40,120
You're not that kind of person.

71
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,199
I've always been this way.

72
00:04:54,319 --> 00:04:55,319
By the way,

73
00:04:56,079 --> 00:04:57,600
this is Black Scorpion's turf.

74
00:04:58,800 --> 00:04:59,959
You'd better behave.

75
00:05:01,079 --> 00:05:02,519
Maybe you should think it through

76
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:05,560
and choose to rely on me.

77
00:05:26,553 --> 00:05:27,553
It's handled?

78
00:05:27,959 --> 00:05:28,959
He's not important.

79
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,720
You're pretty ruthless.

80
00:05:33,439 --> 00:05:34,679
What's your next move?

81
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:35,680
Next,

82
00:05:35,759 --> 00:05:38,079
we wait for Uncle to notify
us of the trade location.

83
00:05:38,279 --> 00:05:39,679
No matter who transports the goods,

84
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:41,279
as long as we have the person,

85
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,199
we have leverage to negotiate.

86
00:05:44,079 --> 00:05:45,439
You're quite the schemer.

87
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,720
Are you backing out?

88
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:50,920
I already agreed to work with you.

89
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,720
Once the goods arrive,

90
00:05:53,079 --> 00:05:54,759
it's the end of the line for that old man.

91
00:06:08,439 --> 00:06:09,480
Lin Yan,

92
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:11,920
you broke your promise.

93
00:06:13,199 --> 00:06:14,279
But I can't.

94
00:06:39,759 --> 00:06:40,759
Why is it here?

95
00:06:42,279 --> 00:06:45,359
I followed the navigation
address Lin Cang left in the car.

96
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:46,360
Did he find out...?

97
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:08,800
Brothers,

98
00:07:08,801 --> 00:07:10,160
I'll take you to see Daddy.

99
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:12,199
You have a dad?

100
00:07:12,319 --> 00:07:13,040
Yeah.

101
00:07:13,041 --> 00:07:14,639
Daddy told me to come pick you up.

102
00:07:15,519 --> 00:07:16,519
Let's go.

103
00:07:16,879 --> 00:07:17,879
Let's go.

104
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:37,360
Oh, right.

105
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,559
I almost forgot.

106
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,439
Daddy reminded me

107
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:40,479
to check if you guys

108
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,560
brought anything with you.

109
00:07:43,399 --> 00:07:44,399
Brought what?

110
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:45,600
Bang, bang, bang!

111
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:50,518
Brother, you have something in your waist.

112
00:07:50,519 --> 00:07:51,560
I saw it.

113
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,638
If you don't give it to
me, Daddy will be mad,

114
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:54,839
and he won't love me anymore.

115
00:07:57,199 --> 00:07:58,199
Just give it to her.

116
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:11,519
I finished my mission!

117
00:08:21,839 --> 00:08:23,638
Sister, I finished my mission!

118
00:08:23,639 --> 00:08:24,639
Good job.

119
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:26,079
Daddy will like you.

120
00:08:28,879 --> 00:08:30,160
Brother Yan, you're here.

121
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:32,559
That's the new orphan Daddy adopted.

122
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:34,319
He said he wanted to
give me a little sister.

123
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:35,399
Isn't she cute?

124
00:08:37,879 --> 00:08:38,879
A-ren,

125
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:40,480
if you want to play,

126
00:08:40,879 --> 00:08:41,919
you can come find me.

127
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:43,440
But,

128
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:45,440
Brother Yan, you're always busy.

129
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,240
But it's okay.

130
00:08:50,399 --> 00:08:52,039
Now I have a little sister to play with.

131
00:08:52,399 --> 00:08:53,678
Daddy has been waiting
for you for a long time.

132
00:08:53,679 --> 00:08:54,679
Come on.

133
00:09:20,039 --> 00:09:21,600
- Uncle.
- Uncle.

134
00:09:26,559 --> 00:09:27,279
A-ren,

135
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,320
go play with A-lian for a bit.

136
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
So,

137
00:09:40,879 --> 00:09:43,558
do you remember this place?

138
00:09:43,559 --> 00:09:45,159
Of course, Uncle.

139
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:47,000
We grew up here.

140
00:09:47,679 --> 00:09:48,679
My parents

141
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:50,320
founded this orphanage.

142
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:54,919
My brother and sister-in-law
were truly good people.

143
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:58,279
It's a pity the good die young.

144
00:09:58,720 --> 00:09:59,839
A-yan,

145
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,679
they entrusted you to me.

146
00:10:01,879 --> 00:10:03,480
I would never harm you.

147
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
A-peng,

148
00:10:08,759 --> 00:10:10,159
I raised you,

149
00:10:10,639 --> 00:10:12,000
and I've always treated you

150
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:14,279
like my own flesh and blood.

151
00:10:15,759 --> 00:10:16,960
Yes, Uncle.

152
00:10:17,639 --> 00:10:18,720
And we

153
00:10:18,879 --> 00:10:20,279
will always remember your kindness.

154
00:10:21,879 --> 00:10:22,879
Uncle,

155
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:25,296
aren't we delivering the goods to
the Black Moon Syndicate today?

156
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:26,559
Are we making the trade here?

157
00:10:29,759 --> 00:10:30,919
No rush.

158
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:33,080
They'll be here a bit later.

159
00:10:39,279 --> 00:10:40,919
Let's play a game first.

160
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:43,399
I'm getting old.

161
00:10:44,279 --> 00:10:45,518
I don't know

162
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:48,000
how you young people play these days.

163
00:10:48,080 --> 00:10:49,080
But,

164
00:10:49,399 --> 00:10:51,159
I should learn a thing or two.

165
00:10:52,799 --> 00:10:54,679
A-peng, you know how.

166
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,120
You deal.

167
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:02,840
I wouldn't say learn.

168
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:06,120
We still rely on you to teach us, Uncle.

169
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:09,560
Since you're interested, Uncle,

170
00:11:09,679 --> 00:11:10,840
I should keep you company.

171
00:11:11,639 --> 00:11:13,399
So, what are we playing?

172
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:22,360
Whatever you say, Uncle.

173
00:11:22,519 --> 00:11:24,399
I'm just afraid the old ways

174
00:11:24,879 --> 00:11:27,679
won't appeal to you young folks.

175
00:11:29,200 --> 00:11:31,639
They'll be replaced sooner or later.

176
00:11:32,919 --> 00:11:34,240
You're joking, Uncle.

177
00:11:34,559 --> 00:11:35,799
Only the classics

178
00:11:36,279 --> 00:11:37,319
make it to the main table.

179
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:39,639
Alright.

180
00:11:39,879 --> 00:11:42,159
Let's play Blackjack then.

181
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:50,679
You're the dealer, you deal.

182
00:11:52,279 --> 00:11:53,840
Look at my memory.

183
00:11:54,519 --> 00:11:55,758
I completely forgot.

184
00:11:55,759 --> 00:11:58,879
I have to deal the cards.

185
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:24,320
I'll stand.

186
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,480
Hit me.

187
00:12:36,120 --> 00:12:37,960
I'll have to trouble you
one more time, Uncle.

188
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:43,960
If you want it, I'll
naturally give it to you.

189
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:47,159
But you need to keep
track of your hole cards.

190
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:49,159
And know when it's right to hit.

191
00:12:52,559 --> 00:12:54,039
You make a good point, Uncle.

192
00:12:54,840 --> 00:12:56,799
Then I'm good here.

193
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,919
Fifteen is enough.

194
00:13:14,159 --> 00:13:15,360
Blackjack.

195
00:13:16,879 --> 00:13:19,240
You stand on seventeen.

196
00:13:19,919 --> 00:13:22,240
You're too scared to hit on fifteen.

197
00:13:22,679 --> 00:13:24,519
Playing like this is no fun.

198
00:13:25,799 --> 00:13:28,000
Hitting on seventeen is an easy bust.

199
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:31,439
So you can only sit on seventeen...

200
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:32,559
...and wait to lose.

201
00:13:48,879 --> 00:13:49,879
Hit.

202
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,279
Looks like you...

203
00:13:55,559 --> 00:13:57,360
...still don't have a strong enough hand.

204
00:13:57,879 --> 00:13:58,639
So...

205
00:13:58,640 --> 00:13:59,678
...I still have to rely on...

206
00:13:59,679 --> 00:14:01,039
...Second Uncle's luck in dealing.

207
00:14:16,399 --> 00:14:17,399
Push.

208
00:14:19,279 --> 00:14:20,558
Same points.

209
00:14:20,559 --> 00:14:21,918
But sitting in different seats...

210
00:14:21,919 --> 00:14:23,079
...leads to different outcomes.

211
00:14:23,080 --> 00:14:25,200
The house takes all.

212
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:28,159
You dare to hit on seventeen?

213
00:14:28,320 --> 00:14:29,200
Aren't you afraid of busting?

214
00:14:29,201 --> 00:14:31,878
It's only seventeen.

215
00:14:31,879 --> 00:14:32,959
If I don't hit...

216
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:35,080
...am I supposed to just
wait for others to win?

217
00:14:36,759 --> 00:14:37,480
What about you?

218
00:14:37,679 --> 00:14:39,639
Too scared to hit on nineteen?

219
00:14:40,159 --> 00:14:41,159
If I hit again...

220
00:14:41,879 --> 00:14:43,399
...the odds of losing are too high.

221
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:46,639
So you'd rather lose...

222
00:14:49,159 --> 00:14:50,600
...than take a gamble.

223
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:54,799
I've never been good at
gambling since I was a kid.

224
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Right.

225
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:59,519
Ever since you were little, you
weren't cut out for gambling.

226
00:15:17,519 --> 00:15:19,399
You've never been
able to keep your cool.

227
00:15:19,759 --> 00:15:21,399
You don't belong at the gambling table.

228
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,080
Hit me.

229
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:31,720
You busted.

230
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,440
If you could hold your nerve...

231
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:36,000
...you might have bet on us both busting.

232
00:15:36,399 --> 00:15:37,799
But now...

233
00:15:38,919 --> 00:15:39,919
Hit.

234
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:47,480
Stand.

235
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:51,559
You're standing already?

236
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:56,679
You stand on nineteen...

237
00:15:56,879 --> 00:15:59,519
...and you're too scared to hit on fifteen.

238
00:16:00,279 --> 00:16:02,360
When will you ever dare to hit?

239
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:04,000
When my hand is strong enough...

240
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:05,879
...or when I have no other choice.

241
00:16:06,385 --> 00:16:09,600
Now isn't the time where
you have no other choice.

242
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:15,000
Blackjack again.

243
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:17,799
I dealt these cards.

244
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:20,120
I make the rules.

245
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:22,079
You don't even dare to hit.

246
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:23,279
How can you possibly beat me?

247
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:26,679
You're right, Second Uncle.

248
00:16:30,919 --> 00:16:33,120
The Black Moon Syndicate isn't coming.

249
00:16:35,919 --> 00:16:37,159
I heard...

250
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:40,360
...someone wants to stab me in the back.

251
00:16:50,399 --> 00:16:52,240
Today's game...

252
00:16:52,519 --> 00:16:53,678
...was just to see...

253
00:16:53,679 --> 00:16:55,999
...who's holding the cards
but is too scared to play them.

254
00:17:02,240 --> 00:17:03,320
Second Uncle.

255
00:17:04,359 --> 00:17:06,559
You don't suspect me, do you?

256
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:09,880
I've been with you since I was twelve.

257
00:17:10,799 --> 00:17:13,278
I've never disobeyed you in the slightest.

258
00:17:13,279 --> 00:17:14,759
Growing up...

259
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:18,599
...all these years have been enough time for
you to breed ambition.

260
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:23,680
Since we're laying it all out...

261
00:17:23,839 --> 00:17:24,839
Second Uncle.

262
00:17:26,119 --> 00:17:28,640
...these are all the men
you have left, right?

263
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:33,039
A-ren.

264
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:34,680
Father, go!

265
00:17:44,200 --> 00:17:45,439
You're not worthy...

266
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:47,079
...to sit at the same table as me.

267
00:17:47,319 --> 00:17:48,319
Kill him.

268
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:53,839
Brother Yan.

269
00:17:53,840 --> 00:17:55,318
Why are you doing this?

270
00:17:55,319 --> 00:17:56,719
How could you betray Father?

271
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:58,160
He's not my father.

272
00:17:58,480 --> 00:17:59,919
He raised you.

273
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:01,439
We're family.

274
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:02,640
You and I are family.

275
00:18:03,279 --> 00:18:04,640
Lin Cang is not.

276
00:18:04,799 --> 00:18:06,640
A-ren, if you see me as your brother...

277
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:08,119
...then don't stop me.

278
00:18:27,839 --> 00:18:28,839
Gunshots.

279
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:30,559
Did the deal go south?

280
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:33,200
I can't betray Father.

281
00:18:36,079 --> 00:18:37,079
Then I'm sorry.

282
00:18:57,599 --> 00:18:58,599
Lin Yan.

283
00:19:00,119 --> 00:19:01,119
Freeze.

284
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:02,880
Unless you want to die.

285
00:19:06,359 --> 00:19:07,479
Let me go after Lin Cang.

286
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:08,679
I'll be too late!

287
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:10,400
Do you really want to be the next Lin Cang?

288
00:19:10,559 --> 00:19:11,680
No matter who I am...

289
00:19:12,039 --> 00:19:13,359
Lin Cang has to die.

290
00:19:13,720 --> 00:19:14,798
Only when he's dead...

291
00:19:14,799 --> 00:19:15,920
...can things change.

292
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:17,720
The change I want...

293
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:19,679
...is for all arms dealers to disappear.

294
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:20,680
Including Lin Cang.

295
00:19:21,759 --> 00:19:22,960
And including you.

296
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:34,640
Can you trust me one more time?

297
00:19:36,880 --> 00:19:38,319
Do you think I'd still trust you?

298
00:19:40,759 --> 00:19:41,880
Let me kill Lin Cang...

299
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,640
...and settle all this first.

300
00:19:45,240 --> 00:19:46,680
I'll do whatever you say after that.

301
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:48,720
Consider it me begging you.

302
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:51,720
Going after him is a suicide mission.

303
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:55,200
I have to go.

304
00:19:57,960 --> 00:19:58,960
Otherwise...

305
00:20:01,240 --> 00:20:02,599
...just kill me right now.

306
00:20:49,359 --> 00:20:50,200
A-yan.

307
00:20:50,359 --> 00:20:52,078
If you just come with me now...

308
00:20:52,079 --> 00:20:54,240
...I'll pretend none of this ever happened.

309
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:56,359
Shut down the whole operation,

310
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:57,999
and I'll go with you.

311
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,160
A-yan.

312
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:02,759
So all these years...

313
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:05,519
...you've hated me this much.

314
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:08,856
Drop your weapon and surrender.

315
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:09,759
The government forces are already here.

316
00:21:09,759 --> 00:21:10,480
You can't escape.

317
00:21:10,599 --> 00:21:11,880
Let's test that theory.

318
00:21:30,759 --> 00:21:32,119
I mean no harm.

319
00:21:37,319 --> 00:21:38,319
Daddy...

320
00:21:44,680 --> 00:21:46,000
I finished my mission!

321
00:22:02,759 --> 00:22:04,680
Big brother, you're a good person.

322
00:22:18,599 --> 00:22:19,680
A-ren.

323
00:22:21,599 --> 00:22:22,880
He never...

324
00:22:23,440 --> 00:22:24,599
...considered himself...

325
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:26,559
...our father.

326
00:22:31,279 --> 00:22:33,000
I will avenge her.
